# Headers for every page (#537); the Content-Security-Policy of each page is in its <meta>, from
# astro.config.mjs. The delete pages act on an account, so no other site may show the site in a
# frame, which only a header can say. The link to delete an account holds its token in the
# fragment, which a referrer never carries, but the site has no reason to send one at all.
# X-Robots-Tag: the legal pages still hold placeholder text, so search engines stay away until it
# is replaced; remove that line before the site goes live.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
